# Alerting-pipeline watch — push to ntfy `yolo-private-cloud-resource-crunch` when the
# ALERTING PIPELINE itself is broken (Prometheus down, Alertmanager down, Watchdog alert
# missing, ntfy webhook failing). Was the resource watcher until 2026-08-04; the resource
# thresholds it owned moved into Alertmanager, which now notifies ntfy directly. This runs
# OUTSIDE the cluster on purpose — it is what still speaks when the cluster is the thing
# that broke, which Alertmanager structurally cannot do for itself.
# Every 5 min; the script debounces (3 consecutive samples = 15 sustained minutes before
# it speaks, then at most hourly, plus one "cleared" note), so this cadence is sampling
# frequency, NOT notification frequency. Cheap: two curls + two instant queries.
*/5 * * * * /home/cloud/Ideaprojects/STEP0/alerting-pipeline-watch.sh >> /home/cloud/Ideaprojects/STEP0/logs/alerting-pipeline-watch.cron.log 2>&1

